{
  "_doc": "IMD meteorological subdivisions (36) defined as unions of Census-2011 districts. Keys are 'State/District' exactly as spelled in the datameet Census_2011 2011_Dist.shp attribute table; 'State/*' means every district of that state. Sub-state splits follow IMD's published subdivision composition, which is revenue-division based for UP / MP / RJ / MH / KA / AP / WB.",
  "_source_shapefile": "datameet/maps Districts/Census_2011/2011_Dist.shp (641 districts, Census 2011 vintage, pre-Telangana-bifurcation)",
  "_caveats": [
    "Census 2011 vintage predates districts created after 2011 (Hapur, Sambhal, Alipurduar, Kalimpong, etc.). Those areas are still covered because the parent district polygon covers them; only the district label is stale. Subdivision-level geometry is therefore unaffected.",
    "Telangana districts sit inside ST_NM='Andhra Pradesh' in this shapefile and are re-assigned here to the TELANGANA subdivision, matching IMD's subdivision list.",
    "Ladakh is inside Jammu & Kashmir; IMD treats it within the J&K subdivision for this vintage."
  ],
